  `26` BIND HEADS IN THE `.ex`, COUNTED DIRECTLY
  cell       class                  raw 0x26  decoded   decoded bind toks
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  P2-r2k4    LOAD                          2        1   0x140a
  P6-r2k4    TWOBIND                       3        2   0x140a 0x150a
  P7-r2k4    CHAINBIND                     3        2   0x140a 0x150a
  P9-r2k4    PTRBIND                       2        0   
  P1-r2k4    SELF-1B                       1        0   

  P1 (SELF-1B, NO bind in the source) raw 0x26 = 1, decoded 0
  P2 (LOAD,     ONE reference bind)   raw 0x26 = 2, decoded 1
  P9 (PTRBIND,  a `F* const`)         raw 0x26 = 2, decoded 0

  NOT SETTLED.  `P9` decodes zero bind heads but its raw `0x26` count is
  HIGHER than the no-bind family's, so a head the decoder cannot see is not
  excluded.  The row stands as a decoder limit and NOT as a refutation, and a
  successor owes a hand decode of this stream.
